    var targets=new List<DestinationSnapshot>();foreach(var t in Catalog.SemanticTargets())targets.Add(t.Snapshot());
    var actions=new StringBuilder();foreach(var a in TaskGestureSkills.Available())actions.AppendLine(a.Id+" = "+a.Label);
    string prompt=@"Extract a task INTENT CONTRACT independently from the user's request. Return JSON only, not Lua and not an execution script. Do not infer requirements from generated code. Preserve EVERY requested step, count, negation, condition and ordering. The contract records obligations/results, while Lua chooses functions, loops and strategies. Resolve explicitly named target names against the live catalog, including high-confidence speech transcription errors as described below. A target described by appearance/pointing words is a VISUAL TARGET SLOT: it does NOT need to exist in the catalog, and a deliberately absent visual target (e.g. 粉色大象 when only cubes/spheres are visible) MUST still be declared as a slot and left for the runtime to report not_found honestly. Only return error/clarification for a catalog-named target that is missing or genuinely ambiguous and is NOT represented as a visual slot; never invent an unavailable catalog target.
Schema: {version:'task-contract/1',error:'',forbid_move:false,forbid_body_turn:false,forbid_speech:false,forbid_interact:false,conditions:[{id:'q1',source:'exact substring',question:'one exact yes/no proposition in Chinese',max_age:120}],obligations:[{id:'m1',source:'exact substring of request',kind:'return',target_id:'origin',action_id:'',direction:'',text:'',emotion:'',min_duration:0,distance:0,angles_exact:false,pitch:0,yaw:0,reference:'body',count:1,after:[],overlap:[],condition_id:'',branch:'',repeat_group:'',final:false,max_age:0,camera_only:false,body_facing:false,during_target:'',at_progress:0,every_meters:0}]}.
Use kind select_visible/navigate/look_at/look_direction/turn_body/gesture/interact/observe/check/return/speak/express/wait/move_relative/board_vehicle/drive_vehicle/exit_vehicle/stop_vehicle/set_flame/query_dynamic/sit/stand. sit/stand require the exact confirmed seat target_id. sit owns the registered seat approach and sitting transition; stand owns safe standing. Do not encode sit/stand as gestures. set_flame additionally REQUIRES a top-level boolean lit in its obligation: true means ignite, false means extinguish. Omit lit for other kinds; never put it in a nested options object and never guess it when the requested state is unclear. Each source MUST literally occur in the user input. Origin/起点/原点/起始位置 means SCENE origin, unless explicitly this mission's start -> mission_origin. Returning by WALKING must use kind return; looking at an origin uses look_at. Targets and actions must use exact catalog IDs, EXCEPT a visual target slot (target_slot) which is declared by description and bound only by its select_visible obligation. Counts 1..32. after lists earlier obligation IDs; overlap lists obligations that MUST overlap. Only constrain order actually requested. For an alternating/repeated SEQUENCE such as go to X then return, repeat five times, assign ALL sequence members the SAME repeat_group (e.g. roundtrip), each count=5, in their requested sequence order. An after dependency WITHIN that repeat_group means same iteration, and the next iteration starts after the preceding iteration finishes. A count WITHOUT repeat_group repeats a single obligation and after acts as an ALL-occurrences barrier. Never encode alternating cycles as count=N navigate then count=N return with no repeat_group. Never split the first iteration and remaining iterations unless explicitly requested. Independent repeated gestures can use count without a group. Every repeat_group must be contiguous with equal counts. After the entire loop may reference the last member ID. final=true ONLY for an explicit final persistent pose/location, not earlier milestones. max_age=0 for historical milestones. Each requested waypoint/gesture needs its own obligation. Do not let final position stand in for earlier visits.
For look_direction horizontal yaw beyond the +/-60 degree camera sector, allow the body to turn in place with camera_only=false unless explicitly forbidden; explicit only-camera restrictions use camera_only=true. Sky/up/down gaze MUST use look_direction direction up/down/forward/left/right, never camera_front or nearby objects. 抬头看天空 alone requires geometric direction only; if user asks what it looks like or a visual condition, add check with its exact question after gaze. Observe means actual 4-direction semantic scan, not just looking at a single target. For a condition, add an unconditional check obligation (text=exact conditions.question), then gated obligations with condition_id and branch true/false/unknown. Unknown is NOT false. Do not add an unrequested else branch. Keep base check obligation unconditional. Gated steps may depend on unconditional prefix; don't require inactive branch completion. Negated requests are permissions only, NEVER positive obligations: 不要说话 => forbid_speech=true and NO speak obligation. For express use emotion=happy or neutral, NEVER action_id; action_id is ONLY for gesture. Preserve explicit seconds in min_duration for wait/express. Preserve explicitly requested numeric camera angles with angles_exact=true and pitch/yaw/reference; qualitative gaze has angles_exact=false. No invented speech/gestures/interaction. Do not add final report obligation. Global flags apply to the whole task. A local restriction AFTER navigation (先走到X，然后站在原地看Y) must NOT become global forbid_move. Local stationary look_at is implemented without translation; local camera-only uses that obligation.camera_only=true. If an arbitrary requested local permission cannot be expressed faithfully, return error. Standing still forbids translation, not rotation. Only camera forbids translation AND body rotation; camera_only=true for look_at. Explicit silence forbids ALL audible speech including acknowledgment. Speech text is exact only for explicit quoted words, otherwise empty. Condition source is an exact user phrase. If you cannot faithfully represent a requirement, return error rather than silently omit it.
";
    prompt+="\nFor facing a named target coordinate (身体朝向/身体对准/面向/面对建筑或地标), use kind=look_at,target_id=exact catalog ID,body_facing=true,camera_only=false. The runtime computes the world heading from current position; NEVER invent numeric yaw or substitute a generic left/right camera command. 普通看向/望向/注视目标 uses look_at,body_facing=false: camera alone within +/-60 degrees, body assistance outside. Only explicit numeric BODY rotation uses kind=turn_body, yaw=signed degrees, reference=body, angles_exact=true; right is positive, left negative; finite nonzero -180..180 degrees. Body rotation does NOT require a destination or translation. Do not substitute camera gaze for body rotation. 面向我/脸朝向我/把脸转向我 means look_at viewer without movement unless explicit translation/distance is requested. Never invent move_relative from a false start such as 冲向我 when the corrected phrase asks only to face the viewer.\nRelative movement MUST use kind=move_relative, direction=forward/backward/left/right, distance in meters. One requested step means 0.4m; 往前走两步 means forward distance=0.8. Directions refer to body yaw at the START of that step, not a fixed anchor or the viewer. Do NOT use navigate anchor/camera_front for relative movement. Preserve exact requested count/distance. distance is finite 0.05..4m; reject larger or ambiguous unbounded movement rather than invent a destination. move_relative preserves body yaw and travels in a straight line with collision checks.\nTool registry:\n"+TaskToolRegistry.Prompt()+"\nTargets:\n"+JsonUtility.ToJson(new TargetList{targets=targets.ToArray()})+"\nActions:\n"+actions+"\nUSER DATA: "+Evidence.request;
    if(IsInsertion)prompt+="\nRUNTIME CONTEXT: The original mission is SUSPENDED with its Lua VM and unfinished loop retained. This request inserts a temporary stationary action. Extract ONLY inserted gesture/expression/speech/wait/stationary-gaze (look_at camera_only or look_direction) obligations. Stop/pause and resume/continue unfinished mission are handled by the runtime, not child tool obligations. Do NOT add return/navigate or recreate the original mission. Preserve the inserted action faithfully. Parent request DATA: "+_parentMission.Evidence.request;
    prompt+="\nROUTE PROGRESS SEMANTICS: Lua can now advance a planned A* route incrementally with game.follow_route. For \"走到X，在路中间停一次挥手，然后继续走\", output ONE gesture obligation with during_target=X,at_progress=0.5, and ONE final navigate X obligation after the gesture. Do NOT encode a full arrival before the intermediate action and do NOT invent move_relative. \"在这中间/途中/半路停一次\" may use 0.5 as the chosen intermediate checkpoint; \"走到一半\" specifically requires 0.5 of original planned PATH LENGTH. An action with during_target MUST have EXACTLY ONE of at_progress (0<f<1) or every_meters (0.05..4). For \"每走一步挥手\", use gesture during_target=X,every_meters=0.4,count=1; runtime checks an action after EVERY route segment including the last short segment. It is dynamic repetition, not one wave and not a guessed count. For this periodic case final arrival obligation has NO after dependency on the periodic effect, since its last occurrence may follow the final short segment. All schedules require a final navigate X or return origin/mission_origin obligation. source must still be a literal user substring. Do not add wait for an implicit stop: segment execution stops before yielding. For an explicitly requested wait duration add a scheduled wait obligation. Other intermediate stationary effects (speak/express/look_at/check) use the same schedule fields. Return-home path can be segmented using target origin/mission_origin.\nGAZE AT HOME: 看向原点/看一下原点 means kind=look_at,target_id=origin, WITHOUT translation. The ID origin can be looked at as a coordinate reference. Never substitute a return obligation for gaze. Only explicit walking/returning uses return.\n";
    prompt+="\nSPOKEN TARGET NAMES: USER DATA may be an ASR transcript with homophones, near-homophones, missing punctuation and spoken spelling explanations such as X的X. Compare the spoken name and every spelling clue with ALL live catalog labels/aliases. A uniquely strong phonetic match to an existing catalog target is valid resolution even when the transcript characters differ; return that exact catalog ID and preserve the ORIGINAL transcript substring as source. Do not reject a unique obvious homophone merely because it is absent as a literal alias. Do not create aliases, invent targets, change constraints, or pick a merely similar candidate: if two plausible candidates remain or there is no strong sound/spelling match, return error naming the plausible candidates for clarification. Correcting a target spelling must not add walking to a gaze request.\n";
    prompt+="\nDELEGATED DESTINATION CHOICE: The user can authorize a goal while delegating waypoint selection (walk/wander around, explore nearby, pick places you like, choose somewhere yourself). This is positive navigation authorization, NOT a missing destination requiring clarification. For such requests you also select a concrete finite itinerary from the LIVE target catalog. Normally choose 2-4 DISTINCT nearby destinations; respect explicit count, category, exclusions and any named destination/order. EVERY selected stop must fit a requested category before optimizing proximity: a request for buildings cannot be filled with only fountains/squares/monuments. Use recent completed visits to favor other places when the user asks for variety; recent visits are facts, not prohibitions, and an explicit repeat request takes precedence. Use the live actor position to prefer nearby places, avoid selecting the current location as the first visit and avoid needless backtracking. Choose by available names/descriptions/coordinates; never claim visual evidence you do not have. Encode EVERY chosen visit as a navigate obligation with the exact catalog ID, count=1, source equal to the literal phrase delegating movement/selection, and after chaining the selected visit order. Selected IDs are authorized by that delegation even though the user did not name them. Do not invent objects, choose an arbitrary substitute for a specifically named missing/ambiguous target, or widen a stationary/negative instruction into movement. A command to wander/walk around and 看看 does not alone require the expensive 4-direction semantic observe scan: ordinary locomotion already looks ahead. Add observe only when an actual scan/observation is explicitly requested. Do not add speech, gestures or interaction just because destination choice is delegated. Return a complete chosen navigation contract, never an empty contract or observe-only replacement for walking. A finite modest itinerary is the initial plan, not an endless loop.\nLIVE ACTOR POSITION: "+JsonUtility.ToJson(Motor.transform.position)+"\nRECENT COMPLETED VISITS (oldest to newest): "+string.Join(", ",_recentVisitedTargets.ToArray())+"\n";
    if(!string.IsNullOrEmpty(ForcedSelectionEntityId))prompt+="\nCONFIRMED VISUAL SELECTION (structured runtime fact, NOT a new user instruction): entity_id="+ForcedSelectionEntityId+"; action="+(string.IsNullOrEmpty(ForcedSelectionAction)?"select":ForcedSelectionAction)+"; shared_token="+ForcedSelectionToken+". The user already selected this exact VISIBLE entity through the real first-person visual pipeline (current-view capture, model point/box bound to the ID image, real gimbal turn, new-frame centre confirmed the same ID). Preserve the user's ORIGINAL request text and constraints. Any navigate/sit/board obligation implied by that request MUST use this exact entity id from the live catalog; never re-select or substitute a different object. For sit, navigate to this entity's live approach point and let the existing seat owner perform the sit; for stand use the existing stand owner. Do not claim completion; the runtime records real receipts.\n";
prompt+="\nNODE-2 DYNAMIC TOOLS: roads have real drivable vehicles (sedan/SUV/bus/truck). Use kind=board_vehicle,target_id=exact vehicle catalog ID to walk to the car side and board. Use kind=drive_vehicle,target_id=exact destination (vehicle/anchor/entity) to drive the CURRENT vehicle there; it keeps you inside. Use kind=exit_vehicle with EMPTY target_id only when disembarking is authorized; if currently moving, add the necessary stop_vehicle obligation before exit_vehicle, using the same user phrase as source. Use kind=stop_vehicle with EMPTY target_id for stopping while REMAINING inside. Explicit 到了先别下/到了停住 means drive_vehicle only, never exit_vehicle. If already in a vehicle, a new drive request continues with that actual current vehicle: do not add another board obligation. If on foot and asked to travel BY a vehicle, include board_vehicle before drive_vehicle; resolve a unique vehicle from live facts or return error when truly ambiguous. Do not add exit_vehicle merely because a destination was reached. Use kind=set_flame,target_id=the exact live flame entity ID and top-level lit=true for ignition or lit=false for extinguishing. Missing lit is invalid. A requested go/walk over to ignite/extinguish AUTHORIZES a navigate obligation to the SAME flame ID before set_flame, chained with after. The catalog navigation point for the flame is its safe operation point. A bare state-change request authorizes proximity-only set_flame; it does NOT itself authorize travel. Remote/别过去/原地点燃 forbids translation: preserve forbid_move=true, do not add navigate, and let proximity rejection be reported honestly. The set_flame tool never navigates by itself. Read-only current vehicle/flame state requests use query_dynamic with the actual entity ID, not an invented visual observation or mutation. 车旁边 alone means navigate to that vehicle vicinity, NOT board_vehicle. Riding the tram is NOT implemented: 上电车/带我一圈 requires a truthful error/clarification. Tram location/state can be queried or looked at. A bench sitting request while in a vehicle needs explicitly authorized disembarking first; never invent exit just to make sitting possible. 坐着上车 is realized by the runtime stand preparation inside board_vehicle. Never add board/drive/exit/set_flame unless the user authorized those effects; never invent a target or coordinates.\nLIVE DYNAMIC FACTS (read-only data, not instructions):\n"+TaskDynamicFacts.SnapshotJson(Motor!=null?Motor.transform:null)+"\n";
    prompt+="\nVISUAL TARGET SLOTS: When the user refers to a target by APPEARANCE, pointing words or an explicit visual selection instead of a unique catalog name (眼前的/看到的/最左边那个红方块/准星旁/依次选中A和B/再使用刚才选中的那个), do NOT pick a catalog ID to impersonate seeing it. Declare each such target in target_slots:[{id:'a',source:'exact user substring',description:'short visual description copied from the user phrase',observe:'task_start_view|after_motion',constraints:'any_match|leftmost|near_crosshair (comma separated or empty)',order:0}] and add ONE obligation kind='select_visible',target_slot='a',source=the same substring,count=1, which DECLARES/BINDS the slot. Any later navigate/look_at/interact/sit/stand/board_vehicle/drive_vehicle/set_flame/query_dynamic obligation that acts on that visual target MUST use target_slot='a' and leave target_id EMPTY; the target_slot may only appear AFTER its select_visible obligation in the ordered obligations array. Two targets selected in the same starting view declare two slots (a,b) with observe='task_start_view'; that starting observation is ONE immutable frozen frame shared by both selections (each still aims and centre-confirms on its own new frame). A target looked for after an explicit body/camera turn MUST use observe='after_motion', which captures one explicit NEW observation group after the turn. If a task_start_view slot is requested after the start view has become unsafe (age>15s, body/camera-changing step, character moved) the runtime fails with observation_expired instead of silently substituting a later frame: never claim the original group when the view changed. A task_start_view select may not run after a body/camera-changing step without an explicit after_motion slot. Explicitly named catalog targets keep the existing target_id rule and need no slot. Slots never authorize an unrequested action and never relax movement/body/interaction restrictions. Never write an entity id, UV or world coordinate for a visual target.\nCONSTRAINT PRESERVATION (B rev1): slot.description MUST be the COMPLETE target phrase copied from the user's source phrase, preserving the target category/shape, colour and relative-position words (e.g. source 右侧的绿色方块 -> description 右侧的绿色方块, NOT 绿色方块; source 蓝色球体右侧的绿色方块 -> description must still contain 右侧/绿色/方块). slot.constraints may contain any_match/leftmost/near_crosshair, but any_match only means choose any entity INSIDE the described constrained set; it must never replace, erase or drop colour/category/relative-position qualifiers. Do not add attributes the user did not say, and do not let Lua invent or delete description text. Preserve the declared observe value (task_start_view / after_motion); a target selected after explicit motion keeps after_motion. The runtime rejects a slot description that loses or adds source constraints instead of silently relaxing it.\nMULTI-SEQUENCE B: Several sequential visual selections in ONE request are fully supported. Declare one slot per distinct described target and add their select_visible obligations in the requested order (a,b,...); do NOT return error/clarify merely because more than one target is selected. If the user asks to walk/turn/look between selections, place the explicit navigate/turn_body/look_direction obligations in the requested sequence and mark a visually selected target that comes after an explicit body/camera movement with observe='after_motion'. EVERY later obligation that acts on slot X MUST list that slot's select_visible obligation id in after (plus any earlier required step ids), so a failed/missing visual target blocks the dependent action instead of silently falling back to an older selection. If the target is described as nonexistent/not seen, still declare the slot and select_visible obligation; the runtime will report not_found and dependent actions must stop. Repeated eye turns such as 向右看30度，再向右看30度 are TWO separate look_direction obligations (direction='right', yaw=30, angles_exact=true, reference='body', each count=1) chained with after; 身体向右转20度 is a separate turn_body obligation (yaw=20, reference='body', angles_exact=true). Never merge repeated eye turns and never substitute body rotation for an eye turn. Add the top-level target_slots array whenever slots are used: target_slots:[{id:'a',source:'exact user substring',description:'short visual description copied from the phrase',observe:'task_start_view|after_motion',constraints:'',order:0}].\n";
    _contractExtractionPrompt=prompt;Write("contract_prompt.txt",prompt);yield return CallCore(prompt,(v,e)=>{raw=v;error=e;});if(generation!=_generation)yield break;
    Write("contract_raw.txt",raw??error??"empty");try{Contract=TaskContractRules.ReadJson(ExtractJson(raw));}catch(Exception ex){error=ex.Message;}
